Legend:
  launch  = mc.launch() — full JIT dispatch every call
  plan    = execute_plan() — cached compilation, device-resident tensors
  graph   = CUDA graph replay — captured stream, zero dispatch overhead
  PyTorch = torch.matmul() on pre-allocated CUDA tensors
  gap     = how many X PyTorch is faster than our best (graph)

At 1024x1024: MatCore graph = 12.1308 TFLOP/s, PyTorch = 17.2296 TFLOP/s
  → PyTorch is 1.4x faster at large sizes (kernel efficiency gap)
  → At small sizes, MatCore graph closes the dispatch overhead gap
  → Closest gap: 1.2x at 1024x1024
